Z||000000||Brian84SE||03-10-2000||07:49 PM||||my headlight motor goes up ok, but going down I have to start it by hand. Then it continues on its own.  Does it just need a good cleaning?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||03-10-2000||09:42 PM||||Check all the relays first, if they're working ok, then it might be that the nylon gear is partially stripped, this is a common problem. To fix it you must open up the motor housing. Sometimes this is riveted, so you have to drill out the rivets and replace them with small bolts. If the gear is stripped, then turn it 180 degrees, only half the gear is used and should still have a good half. There are also aftermarket metal replacement gears. Clean out all the old hardened grease and apply a little bit of new. Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000002||AL||03-10-2000||09:49 PM||||check the contacts inside, also where the contacts make contact, try to get a fine sandpaper and try to clean that also. ||||reg||1
